  "verification_note": "Replaced on 2026-11-05. Seven candidate rewrites adopted (q4, q5, q7, q11, q33, q57, q74) and 23 indexes added, giving 118. Eight runs, two separated passes per scale, 40/40 and zero errors in every run, each asserting \"index set matches sql/ exactly (118 indexes)\". Against the previous configuration: SF=1 139.8->125.4s, SF=2 291.2->241.9s, SF=4 741.2->579.5s, SF=8 2692.2->1599.6s. Measured per query at SF=4 the indexes are worth about -103s alone and the rewrites about -91s on top, so neither half should be credited with the whole gain. Three candidates were rejected: q46 returns 0 rows where the adopted returns 101, q8 is identically empty so equivalence is unproven, q10 measured 1.04x. Raw artifacts committed at experiments/evidence/four_scale_twice_20261105_adopted/ with SHA256SUMS. This configuration is now the default in reproduce.sh. evidence_level, use_in_submission_results and raw_run_artifacts_available left as set: that grading is the report owner's call.",
